Read `AGENTS.md` and `GAME.md` at the repo root before making changes. `AGENTS.md` is the shared contract for every tool (Bailey, ChatGPT,
Cursor, Codex, Claude) and overrides anything else; do not rely on a copy of its rules here. How several tools share the repo:
`docs/ai/WORKFLOW.md`.

Cursor-specific:

- Cloud agents have no Unity editor: run `scripts/test-domain.sh` before every push and report Unity behaviour as unverified.
- Claim your task and branch first (`docs/ai/WORKFLOW.md`), and keep to the files you declared.
